      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>“Remember” by Emma Lazarus was written 20 January 1866 and first published in her chapbook, <tei:hi rend="italic">Poems and Translations</tei:hi> (1866), page 54. The poem was adapted in an abridged form for a hymn by Rabbi J. Leonard Levy in his <tei:hi rend="italic">The Children’s Service for Use in Religious Schools</tei:hi> (1902/1904). (The melody it was adapted for composed by H.S. Cutter as found on page 172 for James Montgomery’s “Solomon’s Prayer for Wisdom” (1860, here entitled “A Wise Heart”).</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_65086_notes"/>
